These issues have been noticed by careful readers of Wave lessons (not by 
me). So as we have feedback we have to somehow reply to it.

#issue 1. Lesson 6 in Waves says: "Other important abstractors include: 
ka...kei (property/aspect abstraction), si'o...kei (concept/idea 
abstraction), ni...kei (quantity abstraction) among others." This sentence 
doesnt explain what si'o/ka/ni mean. Can we change this section of Waves?

#issue 2. Lesson 10 gives such constructs as "pu ku".... but it never 
mentions that ku is a terminator for PU

If you have any ideas how to fix that please reply.

